+
+## Validating a Release End-to-End
+
+After cutting or installing a `hive-cli` gem that touches the tmux launch
+path, validate on a clean install (no manual copying into the installed
+gem):
+
+1. `gem install ./hive-cli-X.Y.Z.gem` (or the release channel), then
+   `hive --version` reports the expected version.
+2. `hive doctor` is green with the Compound Engineering plugin installed.
+3. Run any stage in Claude tmux mode, e.g.
+   `hive run <REPO_ROOT>/.hive-state/stages/2-brainstorm/<task-slug>`:
+   Hive must start Claude, detect the idle prompt, paste the stage prompt,
+   and reach a terminal marker (`WAITING` for brainstorm Q&A) — not
+   `claude_launch_failed` / "can't find pane" (missing wrapper script) and
+   not "claude interactive prompt did not become ready" (detector miss).
+
+### Known issue: daemon/systemd binary drift
+
+A systemd-installed daemon keeps running an older binary until it is
+restarted or upgraded: operators have seen `/usr/bin/hive` at 0.3.1 while
+`~/.local/bin/hive` reports 0.3.2, so daemon-dispatched runs behave per the
+old code even after a manual upgrade. Restart the daemon (`systemctl --user
+restart hive`) or re-run its installer to converge the binaries. This drift
+belongs to the separate local-setup / daemon work — it is NOT caused by (and
+is not fixed by) launcher/detector changes, so do not misattribute launch
+failures on a drifted daemon to this feature area.
