+## claude-tmux - ready-detector tolerance + gem script packaging
+
+**Action:** Fixed the two coupled defects that broke `hive run` in Claude
+tmux mode on a clean install of the 0.3.2 release gem with Claude Code
+2.1.179.
+
+- **Packaging: the interactive wrapper never shipped.** `spec.files` in
+  `hive.gemspec` had no glob for shell scripts, so the built gem omitted
+  `lib/hive/scripts/interactive_claude_wrapper.sh` (and `stop_hook.sh`);
+  `bash <missing-file>` exited instantly and killed the tmux session before
+  Hive could inspect it → `claude_launch_failed` / "can't find pane". Added
+  `lib/hive/scripts/**/*.sh` to `spec.files`. Guarded at two layers:
+  unit-level assertions in `test/unit/gemspec_test.rb`, and a built-gem gate
+  (`test/integration/built_gem_contents_test.rb`) that builds the real `.gem`
+  and asserts every `scripts/*.sh` reference found under `lib/hive/**` exists
+  inside its data payload (references enumerated from source, so future
+  scripts are covered automatically; negative control rebuilds without the
+  glob to prove the assertion can fail).
+- **Detection: the 2.1.179 idle prompt was invisible.** The bare caret now
+  renders as `❯\u00A0` — a non-breaking space Ruby's ASCII-only `\s` does not
+  match — and sits above a separator / caret / separator / footer stack, so
+  both the old matcher and the last-two-nonblank-lines window missed it →
+  "claude interactive prompt did not become ready". `ClaudeLauncher` now
+  matches `❯` followed only by `\p{Zs}`/tab/EOL (`CLAUDE_READY_CARET_LINE`),
+  keeps the trailing-`❯` form, restricts the legacy text-bearing prompt shape
+  (`❯ Try …`) to the last non-blank line, and scans a 10-nonblank-line tail
+  window (`CLAUDE_PROMPT_TAIL_LINES`) instead of pinning a footer distance.
+  Numbered menu carets stay excluded structurally anywhere in the window, so
+  permission / trust / menu fixtures keep rejecting.
+- **Docs:** [[notes/claude-tmux-launch-mode]] gained an end-to-end release
+  validation runbook plus a note that systemd daemons can keep running an
+  older binary until restarted (explicitly out of scope for this fix).
+
+**Verification:** New detector specs accept the hand-authored 2.1.179 NBSP
+fixture (`test/fixtures/panes/ready_prompt_2179_nbsp.txt`) and prior shapes,
+reject permission/trust/menu fixtures, and cover ASCII/NBSP/narrow-NBSP caret
+variants plus footer-distance independence. Gemspec tests pin the packaged
+scripts and a non-empty scripts glob.
+
+**Pages:** [[modules/agent]], [[notes/claude-tmux-launch-mode]]
